{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[e^{7x-4}\\right]$ is the *second derivative* of $e^{7x-4}$.\n\nIn other words, it's the derivative of $\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[e^{7x-4}\\right]$, which is the derivative of $e^{7x-4}$.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[e^{7x-4}\\right]$, we need to differentiate $e^{7x-4}$ twice.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's start by finding $\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[e^{7x-4}\\right]$:\n\n$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[e^{7x-4}\\right]=7e^{7x-4}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[e^{7x-4}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\left(e^{7x-4}\\right)\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(7x-4\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=e^{7x-4}(7)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=7e^{7x-4}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\left(\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\right)\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{2}\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\dfrac{1}{2}\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"Now we can differentiate $7e^{7x-4}$ to find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[e^{7x-4}\\right]$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[e^{7x-4}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[7e^{7x-4}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=49e^{7x-4}\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[e^{7x-4}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[7e^{7x-4}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=7\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[e^{7x-4}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=7\\left(e^{7x-4}\\right)\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(7x-4\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=7e^{7x-4}(7)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=49e^{7x-4}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[e^{7x-4}\\right]=49e^{7x-4}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[e^{7x-4}\\right]$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$49e^{7x-4}$","correct":true},{"content":"$16e^{7x-4}$","correct":false},{"content":"$7e^{7x-4}$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$-16e^{7x}$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
